- The integer array parameter `nums` is sorted in non-decreasing order.
- After executing the method, each unique element in the integer array `nums` appears only once.
- The relative order of the elements in the integer array `nums` is kept the same.
- The result is placed in the first part of the array `nums`.
- The first `k` elements of the array `nums` hold the final result after removing duplicates.
- The length of the integer array `nums` after removing duplicates is equal to `k`.
- The method modifies the input array `nums` in-place with O(1) extra memory.